{
  "raw": {
    "https://jobs.leeds.ac.uk/vacancy.aspx?ref=AHCPR1088": {
      "title": "Lecturer in Philosophy",
      "description": "AHCPR1088 Lecturer in Philosophy - Jobs at the University of Leeds Skip to main content Home Login Register Current Vacancies How to Apply Criminal records Working at Leeds Contact Us FAQs Terms and conditions Terms of use Contact us Accessibility Privacy Cookies Freedom of information Cookies This site requires the use of cookies as defined by our Terms and Conditions . \r\n        We have provided a detailed description of how cookies work and are used on the site . \r\n        To accept cookies, please click the \"Accept Cookies\" button. Accept Cookies Home Login Register Current Vacancies How To Apply Criminal records Working at Leeds Contact Us FAQs Lecturer in Philosophy Are you an ambitious researcher in Philosophy with the ability to carry out world-leading research and deliver an exceptional student experience in a research-intensive Russell Group University? Would you like to join and contribute to a vibrant philosophical community within the interdisciplinary School of Philosophy, Religion and History of Science? The School of Philosophy, Religion, and History of Science at the University of Leeds is seeking an outstanding philosopher with research expertise and teaching experience in moral and/or political philosophy, understood to comprise metanormative theory, moral psychology, normative ethics, political philosophy, and legal philosophy. The successful candidate will lead or direct their own original and independent programme of research at an international standard. The philosophical community within the School is one of the largest and most vibrant in the UK. We have particular research strengths in metaphysics, epistemology, philosophy of science, philosophy of mind, aesthetics, ethics, and political philosophy. Research activity in the area of this post is supported by the Centre for Aesthetic, Moral and Political Philosophy (CAMP). The School has the ambition to be a dynamic and welcoming community renowned for both its academic excellence and its impact on policy, practice, and public life. We value an inclusive working and learning environment and our aim is to develop a diverse staff and student community reflective of this. In addition to the standard online application form that covers the above essential and desirable criteria, please upload the following (in this order) as a single PDF: A standard academic CV; A description of future research plans (1-2 pages), e.g. elaboration of research projects, future publication plans, and/or grant application plans; A recent research writing sample (maximum 10,000 words); *Interviews are to take place on 10 and 11 February 2027* What we offer in return 26 days holiday plus approx.16 Bank Holidays/days that the University is closed by custom (including Christmas) – That’s 42 days a year! Generous pension scheme plus life assurance– the University contributes 14.5% of salary Health and Wellbeing: Discounted staff membership options at The Edge, our state-of-the-art Campus gym, with a pool, sauna, climbing wall, cycle circuit, and sports halls. Personal Development: Access to courses run by our Organisational Development & Professional Learning team. Access to on-site childcare, shopping discounts and travel schemes are also available. And much more! To explore the post further or for any queries you may have, please contact: Prof Pekka Väyrynen, Deputy Head of School (Philosophy and History of Science). Email: p.vayrynen@leeds.ac.uk Email details to a friend Apply Online Share: View All Vacancies Job Details Location Leeds - Main Campus Faculty/Service Faculty of Arts, Humanities & Cultures School/Institute School of Philosophy, Religion & History of Science Category Academic Grade Grade 8 Salary £51,753 to £59,966\r\n              p.a. Working Time 100% Post Type Full Time Contract Type Ongoing Release Date Thursday 15 October 2026 Closing Date Sunday 22 November 2026 Reference AHCPR1088 Downloads Candidate Brief (PDF) Apply Online Search Jobs Keyword Search: Search Existing Account / Staff Member Do you have an existing account, or are you a member of staff? Login New User For new applicants, please register for an account Register © 2026 University of Leeds | Terms and conditions | Terms of use | Contact us | Accessibility | Privacy | Cookies | Freedom of information"
    },
    "https://jobs.leeds.ac.uk/vacancy.aspx?ref=EPSEE1162": {
      "title": "Lecturer in Electronic and Electrical Engineering (T&R) (1 post)",
      "description": "EPSEE1162 Lecturer in Electronic and Electrical Engineering (T&R) (1 post) - Jobs at the University of Leeds Skip to main content Home Login Register Current Vacancies How to Apply Criminal records Working at Leeds Contact Us FAQs Terms and conditions Terms of use Contact us Accessibility Privacy Cookies Freedom of information Cookies This site requires the use of cookies as defined by our Terms and Conditions . \r\n        We have provided a detailed description of how cookies work and are used on the site . \r\n        To accept cookies, please click the \"Accept Cookies\" button. Accept Cookies Home Login Register Current Vacancies How To Apply Criminal records Working at Leeds Contact Us FAQs Lecturer in Electronic and Electrical Engineering (T&R) (1 post) Do you have a track record of high quality research and a clear vision for developing your profile at an international level? Can you contribute to innovative research led teaching and support an excellent student experience across undergraduate and postgraduate programmes? Are you committed to working collaboratively, contributing to an inclusive and supportive School community, and engaging in active academic citizenship? Applications submitted during the previous recruitment campaign will not be reconsidered. Previous applicants may submit a new application if they can demonstrate additional relevant skills, experience, or achievements not included in their original application All staff are responsible for upholding the University's Values, including contributing to an environment in which everyone is free from discrimination and harassment, and diverse voices and experiences are actively included. We are seeking to appoint a Lecturer in Power Electronics who will contribute to the School of Electronic and Electrical Engineering’s academic mission through research, teaching, and academic citizenship. The successful applicant will be able to teach in core areas of Electronic and Electrical Engineering with a research focus at the frontier of power electronics and its integration with power systems. We are particularly interested in candidates with expertise in inverter-based resources (IBRs), the integration of IBRs into power systems, grid-forming and grid-following converter control, and the stability, dynamics, and control of power-electronics-dominated networks. This post will join a highly successful group carrying out research into renewable energy technologies which is contributing to the national and international activities for net zero. The successful candidate would join the Institute of Communication and Power Networks (ICaPNet). This role offers the opportunity to develop and sustain a high quality, internationally recognised research programme aligned with the School’s strategic priorities, including active engagement in collaborative, interdisciplinary, and externally funded research. You will deliver research informed teaching across undergraduate and postgraduate programmes, contributing to curriculum design, innovation, and enhancement. You will play a key role in fostering an inclusive, engaging, and high quality student experience, and will support the academic and professional development of students and early career researchers through effective supervision and mentoring. In addition, you will contribute to the effective and collegial operation of the School through administrative and service activities, working collaboratively with colleagues and supporting the University’s commitment to excellence, equity, diversity, and inclusion. The role may also include teaching or academic engagement in support of the School’s transnational education activities, including overseas teaching for up to six weeks in an academic year. What we offer in return 26 days holiday plus approx.16 Bank Holidays/days that the University is closed by custom (including Christmas) – That’s 42 days a year! Generous pension scheme plus life assurance– the University contributes 14.5% of salary Generous pension scheme options plus life assurance Health and Wellbeing: Discounted staff membership options at The Edge, our state-of-the-art Campus gym, with a pool, sauna, climbing wall, cycle circuit, and sports halls. Personal Development: Access to courses run by our Organisational Development & Professional Learning team. Access to on-site childcare, shopping discounts and travel schemes are also available. And much more! To explore the post further or for any queries you may have, please contact: Professor Kevin Morris, Head of the School of Electronic and Electrical Engineering Email: K.Morris1@leeds.ac.uk Please note that this post may be suitable for sponsorship under the Skilled Worker visa route but first-time applicants might need to qualify for salary concessions. For more information please visit: www.gov.uk/skilled-worker-visa . For research and academic posts, we will consider eligibility under the Global Talent visa. For more information, please visit the Government’s page, Apply for the Global Talent visa. Email details to a friend Apply Online Share: View All Vacancies Job Details Location Leeds - Main Campus Faculty/Service Faculty of Engineering & Physical Sciences School/Institute School of Electronic & Electrical Engineering Category Academic Grade Grade 8 Salary £51,753 to £59,966\r\n              per annum Working Time 100% Post Type Full Time Contract Type Ongoing Release Date Monday 26 October 2026 Closing Date Friday 20 November 2026 Reference EPSEE1162 Downloads Candidate Brief (PDF) Apply Online Search Jobs Keyword Search: Search Existing Account / Staff Member Do you have an existing account, or are you a member of staff? Login New User For new applicants, please register for an account Register © 2026 University of Leeds | Terms and conditions | Terms of use | Contact us | Accessibility | Privacy | Cookies | Freedom of information"
    },
    "https://jobs.leeds.ac.uk/vacancy.aspx?ref=FBSBM1240": {
      "title": "Associate Professor in Exercise Physiology",
      "description": "FBSBM1240 Associate Professor in Exercise Physiology - Jobs at the University of Leeds Skip to main content Home Login Register Current Vacancies How to Apply Criminal records Working at Leeds Contact Us FAQs Terms and conditions Terms of use Contact us Accessibility Privacy Cookies Freedom of information Cookies This site requires the use of cookies as defined by our Terms and Conditions . \r\n        We have provided a detailed description of how cookies work and are used on the site . \r\n        To accept cookies, please click the \"Accept Cookies\" button. Accept Cookies Home Login Register Current Vacancies How To Apply Criminal records Working at Leeds Contact Us FAQs Associate Professor in Exercise Physiology Associate Professor in Exercise Physiology Are you an experienced and influential academic with the proven ability to carry out teaching and research in exercise physiology and related topics? Do you have an excellent research track record, proven success obtaining funding and the vision and drive to tackle new challenges? Are you passionate about delivering world leading research and an exceptional student experience? As Associate Professor, you will carry out research, teaching and management within the school, faculty and university and contribute to academic leadership in the field of biomedical and sport and exercise science. You will join a vibrant, supportive, and highly collaborative Cardiovascular and Exercise Sciences research pillar. The pillar has an established international reputation for research spanning cardiovascular, respiratory, and musculoskeletal physiology using experimental human, clinical and computational approaches. The research extends from fundamental discovery science to translational application, investigating physiological mechanisms and developing innovative approaches to improve health, recovery and rehabilitation We welcome applications from candidates whose research will complement and extend our existing portfolio. We are particularly interested in applicants whose research advances our understanding of the physiological responses and adaptations to exercise and other forms of physiological stress, with applications in healthy ageing, disease prevention, and the treatment and rehabilitation of people living with acute and chronic health conditions. You will establish and lead an independent research programme, securing competitive external research funding and developing interdisciplinary collaborations within and beyond the University. You will contribute to innovation and excellence in teaching, supervise and develop postgraduate researchers, and provide academic leadership and mentorship to colleagues. This role offers an exciting opportunity to shape the future of exercise physiology at Leeds and deliver research with international reach and impact. The School sits within the newly formed Faculty of Health and Life Sciences, bringing together fundamental and clinical scientists with access to outstanding research infrastructure, from state-of-the-art laboratory facilities and specialist equipment to strong partnerships with Leeds Teaching Hospitals NHS Trust. What we offer in return • 26 days holiday plus approx.16 Bank Holidays/days that the University is closed by custom (including Christmas) – That’s 42 days a year! • Generous pension scheme options plus life assurance. • Health and Wellbeing: Discounted staff membership options at The Edge, our state-of-the-art Campus gym, with a pool, sauna, climbing wall, cycle circuit, and sports halls. • Personal Development: Access to courses run by our Organisational Development & Professional Learning team. • Access to on-site childcare, shopping discounts and travel schemes are also available. And much more! To explore the post further or for any queries you may have, please contact: Elaine Martin Interim Head of the School of Biomedical Sciences Email: E.Martin@leeds.ac.uk Ronaldo Ichiyama Director of Research and Innovation School of Biomedical Sciences Email: R.M.Ichiyama@leeds.ac.uk Email details to a friend Apply Online Share: View All Vacancies Job Details Location Leeds - Main Campus Faculty/Service Faculty of Biological Sciences School/Institute School of Biomedical Sciences Category Academic Grade Grade 9 Salary £61,759 to £73,708\r\n              per annum Post Type Full Time Contract Type Ongoing Release Date Thursday 22 October 2026 Closing Date Thursday 19 November 2026 Reference FBSBM1240 Downloads Candidate Brief (PDF) Apply Online Search Jobs Keyword Search: Search Existing Account / Staff Member Do you have an existing account, or are you a member of staff? Login New User For new applicants, please register for an account Register © 2026 University of Leeds | Terms and conditions | Terms of use | Contact us | Accessibility | Privacy | Cookies | Freedom of information"
    },
    "https://jobs.leeds.ac.uk/vacancy.aspx?ref=AHCLH1013": {
      "title": "Director of the Leeds Arts and Humanities Research Institute",
      "description": "AHCLH1013 Director of the Leeds Arts and Humanities Research Institute - Jobs at the University of Leeds Skip to main content Home Login Register Current Vacancies How to Apply Criminal records Working at Leeds Contact Us FAQs Terms and conditions Terms of use Contact us Accessibility Privacy Cookies Freedom of information Cookies This site requires the use of cookies as defined by our Terms and Conditions . \r\n        We have provided a detailed description of how cookies work and are used on the site . \r\n        To accept cookies, please click the \"Accept Cookies\" button. Accept Cookies Home Login Register Current Vacancies How To Apply Criminal records Working at Leeds Contact Us FAQs Director of the Leeds Arts and Humanities Research Institute This job is only available to University of Leeds staff.  It may be released externally should we not appoint internally. Opportunity open to existing Grade 9 / Grade 10 academics within the Faculty of Arts, Humanities and Cultures at the University of Leeds only. The long-established Leeds Arts and Humanities Research Institute (LAHRI) plays a key role in developing, promoting and supporting outstanding interdisciplinary research within and beyond the Faculty of Arts, Humanities and Cultures. Its approach and schemes continue to develop in line with the University’s strategy and priorities, and in response to, and anticipation of, changing external contexts. As LAHRI Director, you will work closely with Research and Innovation Services (RIS), the Faculty Research and Innovation Office (FRIO) and University institutes to support the development of excellent, impact-oriented research that draws on and showcases the wide range of Arts and Humanities disciplines represented within and beyond the Faculty. An important part of the role will be to support the development of ambitious, high-quality external funding applications, assessing and improving the effectiveness of LAHRI's training and research-development support in strengthening applications and contributing to funding success. You will be a member of the Faculty Research and Innovation Committee and other relevant bodies, such as the Cultural Institute Steering Group. You will report to the Associate Pro Vice Chancellor (APVC) for Research and Innovation (FAHC) and work closely with them to deliver the Faculty’s research and innovation priorities. You will also report regularly to the Faculty Executive Committee. You will play a vital role in building capability for interdisciplinary research. Supported by the Arts and Humanities Research and Innovation Development Manager, you will strengthen academic networks and build vibrant research communities across schools and faculties, generating ambitious new research ideas and agendas. You will work where appropriate with the Horizons Institute, Leeds Institute for Societal Futures and the Digital Creativity and Cultures Hub and connect with arts and humanities researchers beyond Leeds. You will play an active role in translating these ideas and collaborations into ambitious, competitive external funding applications, particularly larger-scale and interdisciplinary bids. You will also help to showcase high-quality interdisciplinary research projects, outputs and impacts, celebrating success both within the University and externally. A further priority will be to develop research relationships and networks with international partners, particularly the key strategic partners identified by the APVC International. To explore the post further, or for any queries you may have, please contact: Professor Beth Johnson Associate Pro-Vice-Chancellor: Research and Innovation, Faculty of Arts, Humanities and Cultures Email: b.l.johnson@leeds.ac.uk Email details to a friend Apply Online View All Vacancies Job Details Location Leeds - Main Campus Faculty/Service Faculty of Arts, Humanities & Cultures School/Institute Leeds Humanities Research Institute Category Academic Grade Grade 9\r\n              \r\n                to Grade 10 Salary Allowance of £4,775 a year (non-recurrent, non-pensionable) Working Time 60% fte Post Type Part Time Contract Type Fixed Term (three years in the first instance) Release Date Monday 26 October 2026 Closing Date Sunday 08 November 2026 Interview Date To be confirmed Reference AHCLH1013 Downloads Candidate Brief (PDF) Apply Online Search Jobs Keyword Search: Search Existing Account / Staff Member Do you have an existing account, or are you a member of staff? Login New User For new applicants, please register for an account Register © 2026 University of Leeds | Terms and conditions | Terms of use | Contact us | Accessibility | Privacy | Cookies | Freedom of information"
    },
    "https://jobs.leeds.ac.uk/vacancy.aspx?ref=AHCFO1080": {
      "title": "Faculty Director of Equity, Diversity and Inclusive Excellence",
      "description": "AHCFO1080 Faculty Director of Equity, Diversity and Inclusive Excellence - Jobs at the University of Leeds Skip to main content Home Login Register Current Vacancies How to Apply Criminal records Working at Leeds Contact Us FAQs Terms and conditions Terms of use Contact us Accessibility Privacy Cookies Freedom of information Cookies This site requires the use of cookies as defined by our Terms and Conditions . \r\n        We have provided a detailed description of how cookies work and are used on the site . \r\n        To accept cookies, please click the \"Accept Cookies\" button. Accept Cookies Home Login Register Current Vacancies How To Apply Criminal records Working at Leeds Contact Us FAQs Faculty Director of Equity, Diversity and Inclusive Excellence This job is only available to University of Leeds staff.  It may be released externally should we not appoint internally. Opportunity open to existing Grade 9 / Grade 10 academics within the Faculty of Arts, Humanities and Cultures at the University of Leeds only. The Faculty has a strong commitment to Equity, Diversity and Inclusion (EDI) as an integral part of its academic mission, culture and ways of working. The Faculty Director of Equity, Diversity and Inclusive Excellence provides senior academic leadership for this agenda across the Faculty and its nine Schools, working closely with the Faculty’s Executive Team, Heads of School, School EDI Leads, the Faculty EDI Officer and relevant University colleagues. The Director is responsible for driving the strategic direction, promoting a coherent Faculty-wide approach and ensuring that EDI priorities are evidence-led, proportionate and aligned with Faculty and University strategy, including the One Leeds agenda. The Director provides functional leadership to the EDI Leads within each of the Faculty's Schools, while Heads of School retain formal line-management responsibility for those roles. A major responsibility of the Director is the academic and strategic leadership of the Faculty's Athena Swan programme. The immediate priority is to lead the Faculty's Athena Swan Silver application, due for submission in July 2027. To explore the post further or for any queries you may have, please contact: Professor Kristyn Gorton, Deputy Pro-Vice-Chancellor Email: K.Gorton@leeds.ac.uk Email details to a friend Apply Online View All Vacancies Job Details Location Leeds - Main Campus Faculty/Service Faculty of Arts, Humanities & Cultures School/Institute Faculty Office Category Academic Grade Grade 9\r\n              \r\n                to Grade 10 Working Time 0.6 fte Post Type Part Time Contract Type Fixed Term (12 months) Release Date Tuesday 27 October 2026 Closing Date Sunday 08 November 2026 Interview Date To be confirmed Reference AHCFO1080 Downloads Candidate Brief (PDF) Apply Online Search Jobs Keyword Search: Search Existing Account / Staff Member Do you have an existing account, or are you a member of staff? Login New User For new applicants, please register for an account Register © 2026 University of Leeds | Terms and conditions | Terms of use | Contact us | Accessibility | Privacy | Cookies | Freedom of information"
